  "goodToKnow": "Die Kundgebung is a rally, usually a stationary gathering with speeches, while a Demonstration or Demo often marches through the streets. Freedom of assembly is guaranteed by Article 8 of the Grundgesetz; rallies must normally be registered with the authorities beforehand. In early 2024, huge Kundgebungen against right-wing extremism drew over a million people across Germany. The word comes from kundgeben (to make known), from the old word kund (known)."
